{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan","id":14531,"title":"the Samedi: a replacement Lineage for the Ulgan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-19T21:58:06-08:00","id":14531,"title":"the Samedi: a replacement Lineage for the Ulgan","content":"Something about the Ulgan has always rubbed me the wrong way. While the other Lineages all seemed familiar on some level the Ulgan were utterly strange and almost felt out of place in the world of Promethean. Recently while reading a thread someone suggested a Lineage based on zombie myths instead and that inspired me to create this replacement Lineage for my next game (Ulgan's will not be used, these guys will instead). Enjoy! <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>Samedi - the Risen</u></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Description:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The line between shaman and madman is a thin one, should the line exist at all. Their bodies pumped full of psychotropic drugs and buried beneath the dirt, the Samedi rise from the generative ritual with one foot in both worlds; the mortal and the spirit. While they might claim, or dearly wish, otherwise, the spirits most often called to the Samedi and with whom the Samedi most often traffic are those of the dead.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This wears on them. Rejected by living mortals and surrounded by the shades of the dead, the Risen\u2019s relationship with humanity is complicated by their proximity to mortality. Not quite alive or dead themselves Samedi spend as much time thinking about the end of mortal existence as they do the beginning of it. The Risen\u2019s proximity to finality and the termination of mortal existence sometimes even makes them a pariah amongst the other Created who pursue mortality largely ignoring the existential crisis that the Samedi address daily.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Their bodies suffused with potent intoxicants that provided the alchemical impetus for their creation their odd behavior and mannerisms may as much be the result of their drug addled organs as it is their perception of the spirit world. Frequently the odd behavior and idiosyncrasies of the Risen can be as much ascribed to their internal alchemy as to their supernatural ability to communicate with the dead and other spirits. Redeemed Samedi are as likely to end up involved in drug trade or a victim of addiction as they are becoming mystics or the devoutly spiritual.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Nicknames:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">the Risen, Zombies (usually taken as an insult)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Appearance:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">While the Lineage began on the west coast of Africa it has since spread across the world and the Risen make no judgments about race or<br /> appearance when performing the generative ritual on another. Despite this lack of unifying physical appearance, the Samedi frequently have a wild look about them as if they are hearing or seeing things that no one else does - even other Risen.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Disfigurement:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When their Disfigurement is laid bare, Samedi appear to have leathered skin and the eyes of the Risen sink so far into the back of the head that they are always shadowed by the brow. The air around the Samedi, which always has a bit of an odd smell, hangs heavy with the stink of putrid intoxicants. Across the tight skin of the Samedi a pale mist rises and from open cuts it pours profusely into the air.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Humour:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ectoplasmic (intuitive, instinctual)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Element:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Spirit, sometimes known as aether to alchemists, is the ruling element of the Samedi. To regain Pyros by communing with his element, a Samedi must imbibe enough intoxicants or poisons that a mortal his size would become at least moderately inebriated.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Bestowment:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ephemeral Flesh, Re-Animator (the animated corpse must have died while intoxicated)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Disquiet, Wasteland, Torment:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">All as the Ulgan Lineage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Refinements:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Depending on their relationship with their nature, Samedi tend towards either Aurum (if they wish to flee their supernatural half and focus solely on their mortal nature) or Argentum (if they wish to flee the mortal half of their nature and focus solely on their supernatural nature). A Risen who is more at peace with the dual nature of his existence will likely try Cuprum, Mercurius, or Plumbum.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Character Creation:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Among the Samedi there are few patterns of real note. Samedi with physical inclinations tend to see themselves as warriors positioned between the living and the dead while those with social leanings tend more towards acting as a medium or facilitator. Intellectually endowed Samedi instead focus on the existential consequences of their nature and act as advisors to their throngmates.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Concepts:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">medium, shaman, mouth of the dead, exorcist, investigator, chemist, botanist, drug dealer</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Quote:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cPlease don\u2019t call me the z-word.\u201d</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T00:29:06-08:00","id":14565,"title":"","content":"God, yes. I am so grateful for this. The Ulgan have always sat poorly with me and these feel like a fine replacement, Great work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T02:19:54-08:00","id":14602,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't reuse the Uglan Disquiet/Wasteland. The Uglan are spirit focused not Ghost focused, and it's Ghosts and mortality that really contribute to exploring humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T08:23:22-08:00","id":14715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=14602#post14602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't reuse the Uglan Disquiet/Wasteland. The Uglan are spirit focused not Ghost focused, and it's Ghosts and mortality that really contribute to exploring humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read the rules on the Ulgan wasteland in a while, but it could be fairly easy to convert from spirits to ghosts. Themes would be changed, but rules should be pretty close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T14:26:45-08:00","id":14881,"title":"","content":"As much as I adore the Ulgan, these guys fill a void I've wanted in Promethean conceptually far better in my mind. Ghosts, the human dead, the nature of the soul, the afterlife; these are -major- components in understanding what it is to be human in the WoD (and some of them in general when it comes to the Big Questions of humankind). Lots of potential to work with here.<br /> <br /> The Ulgan wasteland would be an easy conversion, but borrowing the elements from Book of the Dead on the Underworld descriptors and having them bleed through into the lands of the living would be a good way to start. Better yet... The Land of Worms. They get the most detail in Ancient Bloodlines for V:tR, but these would be a spectacular basis for a Samedi wasteland even if they're not entirely alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T15:17:15-08:00","id":14900,"title":"","content":"Agreed: a Lineage that focuses on ghosts and the dead is <i>so</i> much more appropriate to <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s thematic focus on the human condition than a focus on animistic spirits is that if <b>Promethean</b> ever gets a Chronicle book, I think the Ulgans should be retooled to be primarily oriented toward ghosts rather than spirits. I think that all three of Disquiet, Wasteland, and Torment need tweaking to be suitable for ghosts rather than spirits; but the amount of tweaking needed should be relatively minor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T15:38:23-08:00","id":14915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=14900#post14900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Ulgans should be retooled to be primarily oriented toward ghosts rather than spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stridently disagree, because we <i>have</i> a Lineage that's suitable for dealing with ghosts and the dead <i>and it's the Nepri.</i> Both of their main Bestowments revolve around death, they claim descent from a king of the dead, and their dominant humor fits better with the dead than the ectoplasmic humor in terms of temperament and thematic imagery. The signature Osiran's pet project wasn't picked out of a hat.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that we have a Lineage for zombi folklore and it's the Tammuz; I'm kind of confused how one gets to a creation ritual that includes &quot;bury the body in the earth&quot; without recognizing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-20-2013, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:39:51-08:00","id":14962,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve posted my thoughts on this in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages\">a separate thread</a>, as it deals with more than just the ghost-based Lineage. But just let me note here that all five of the core Lineages deal with humans getting killed and new life being imbued into their corpses. What this Lineage brings to the table isn\u2019t so much the zombie aspect as it is the <i>ghost</i> aspect.<br /> <br /> Benjamin: I\u2019d suggest that some renaming may be in order here. Each of the other Lineages is named after its supposed Progenitor (or, in the Frankensteins\u2019 case, the demiurge who created their Progenitor), and has an alternate name. \u201cSamedi\u201d comes from Voodoo mythology, where he\u2019s the loa in charge of death; is that really the name you want associated with this Lineage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-20-2013, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:46:40-08:00","id":14966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=14962#post14962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve posted my thoughts on this in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages\">a separate thread</a>, as it deals with more than just the ghost-based Lineage. But just let me note here that all five of the core Lineages deal with humans getting killed and new life being imbued into their corpses. What this Lineage brings to the table isn\u2019t so much the zombie aspect as it is the <i>ghost</i> aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as somebody who has a running gag about drawing illusory connections I'm going to point out that the OP makes no mention of ghosts whatsoever and has said nothing for or against the ghost discussion that's sprung up in the comments here, so ascribing intent is rather premature.<br /> <br /> Beard, care to weigh in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:25:06-08:00","id":15132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=14602#post14602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't reuse the Uglan Disquiet/Wasteland. The Uglan are spirit focused not Ghost focused, and it's Ghosts and mortality that really contribute to exploring humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I did this pretty quick and dirty and was planning to edit out references to wider spirits in my personal games, yes, you're right that narrowing in on the dead is probably going to help push the Samedi further in the direction that I would want them to go. Other posters had it right that it may be as simple as just using Ulgan themes but removing animist spirits and leaving in the spirits of the dead but for completion's sake I will write up descriptions of what exactly that looks like and post them here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:34:19-08:00","id":15140,"title":"","content":"I agree with Satchel - I think it's great that people customize these games to fit their preferences, but I don't see what this lineage adds to the game and how they're more interesting than the Ulgan.<br /> <br /> The being torn apart by spirits is a pretty interesting thematic angle, I'd hate to see it go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:40:23-08:00","id":15148,"title":"","content":"Responding to both Satchel and Dataweaver...<br /> <br /> On the Nepri and their relationship to the dead - I suppose you're right that Corpse Tongue somewhat positions them as mediums. I don't think Revivification does as their own immortality does not really equate to them having relationship with the dead. Really even Corpse Tongue doesn't suggest that the Nepri can communicate with the dead so much as extract information from corpses. It doesn't seem to mention contacting the spirit itself. Still, I see what you mean and you're right that there is some overlap there. My preference would probably be to scale back some of that theme in the Nepri to allow space for the Samedi since, honestly, I can't stand Ulgans but I really want a 5th core lineage.<br /> <br /> On the name, Samedi - I actually think it fits quite well and I am happy for their mythology to suggest that Samedi is their Progenitor. I admit to not being super well versed in African folklore or religion but a brief excerpt from wikipedia kind of hits on a lot of the exact themes I was going for with the Lineage. Check out the Portrayal tab; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Samedi\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Samedi</a>.<br /> <br /> On the intent to have Samedi have relationships with ghosts - yes. While it is not spelled out explicitly in the Lineage write up as is (instead it makes oblique references to &quot;the dead&quot; and refers to them as mediums and speakers for the dead) that was definitely my intention. I don't understand how communing with animist spirits is really in the theme of becoming a mortal (i.e. the Ulgans) but regularly confronting mortality seems pretty in theme (these guys).<br /> <br /> Would have loved to have been more eloquent in this response but I am exhausted!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:52:37-08:00","id":15155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=15140#post15140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Satchel - I think it's great that people customize these games to fit their preferences, but I don't see what this lineage adds to the game and how they're more interesting than the Ulgan.<br /> <br /> The being torn apart by spirits is a pretty interesting thematic angle, I'd hate to see it go.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually exactly what I dislike about the Ulgan. A huge part of their generative process includes this thing that is not Demiurge, Promethean, the Principle, or Divine Fire but spirits. Which spirits are these that know how to create Prometheans? What are they doing when they're not creating Prometheans? Why do they want to create Prometheans? And even if all those questions have reasonable answers, it seems to really dilute the theme of the game to have 4 Lineages that are mostly focused on mortals and their relationship to them and then this 5th one that is hooked into all kinds of supernatural shenanigans a la animist spirits. In my experience of running Promethean the game is a love letter to the human condition and Ulgans make no interesting comment in that respect (in my opinion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T23:24:27-08:00","id":15172,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Benjamin Beard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=15155#post15155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which spirits are these that know how to create Prometheans?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spirits that are summoned by a particular type of call and which are compelled to shred physical matter that is in Twilight to send it back&quot; are not &quot;spirits that know how to create Prometheans&quot; and I'm kind of baffled that anyone could make that mistake since they're a glorified wood-chipper.<br /> <br /> Strange Alchemies covers this:</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;The spirits know what this is. It is part of their intrinsic nature to understand this rite, for it is as old as they are. They rip apart the body, filthy matter left in the world of spirit. They hate its presence there, and they know that if they rend it, the shaman will snatch it back through. It is an old chiminage.&quot;</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are they doing when they're not creating Prometheans? </div> </div> </div>What spirits normally do, frankly. Tending their purviews and advancing their agendas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do they want to create Prometheans? </div> </div> </div>They don't. See above for my bafflement at how one could reach the conclusion that they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even if all those questions have reasonable answers, it seems to really dilute the theme of the game to have 4 Lineages that are mostly focused on mortals and their relationship to them and then this 5th one that is hooked into all kinds of supernatural shenanigans a la animist spirits. </div> </div> </div>The Lineage that's all about getting away from the supernatural duty foisted on them, shockingly enough, has plenty to do with the game about trying to stop being a supernatural being, particularly when it hooks into a cultural role that's historically entailed both bridging the human and supernatural worlds and being made to live on the edges of human society.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-21-2013, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T23:33:17-08:00","id":15176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=15172#post15172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't. See above for my bafflement at how one could reach the conclusion that they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people might read your repeated bafflement at others reaching conclusions other than the one you've reached as kind of condescending. Just saying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T23:34:17-08:00","id":15177,"title":"","content":"So I've kind of cheated and basically still used the Riven Wasteland because it's description is so meager it seemed silly to rephrase in detail. Other than that, here is at least a Samedi specific Disquiet and Torment.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Disquiet:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In the early stages of Disquiet the Samedi inspires the mortals around him to feel regret and loss more keenly. Mortals in the throes of early stages of Disquiet notice that when the Samedi is around they seem to fixate on those that have already passed and the unfinished business they had with them. As Disquiet grows mortals\u2019 thinking begins to take mad leaps of logic, noticing mannerisms that the Samedi displays that they attribute to a deceased friend or family. Events seem to be filled with meaning and omen to these mortals and even the most rational humans become superstitious that the dead have come back to contact them. Increasingly those infected with the Samedi Disquiet believe that they are being haunted by the dead and that the Samedi is in some way responsible or the vector of this haunting. Beyond even this mortals affected by the Samedi Disquiet sense that the Samedi is in some way a walking avatar of existential finality and that his presence in the area in some way foreshadows great loss - a loss mortals are keen to avoid by driving out or destroying the Risen.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wasteland:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As Riven Wastelands save that the spirits are the spirits of the dead rather than the spirits of Twilight generally.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Torment:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When a Samedi Promethean enters Torment he becomes obsessed with the past lives of those ghosts he has communicated with, mortals who he has known and who have died or the past life of the body he currently possesses. Desperately attempting to put the mortal lifetime in context and create meaning the Risen is compelled to complete tasks left undone by those who have passed. While in Torment the needs and the desires of the living seem like small things compared to those who are already gone from the world. While suffering from Torment the Samedi has a -1 penalty on Manipulation rolls as the Risen focuses intently on fulfilling the (real or imagined) wishes of the dead rather than maintaining social niceties.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:05:24-08:00","id":15186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Benjamin Beard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=15176#post15176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some people might read your repeated bafflement at others reaching conclusions other than the one you've reached as kind of condescending. Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware, though the sting of such assessments is rather blunted in those situations where &quot;reaching the conclusion Satchel reached&quot; is directly synonymous with &quot;reading the text that is actually written in the books instead of interpolating fabrications that happen to be easier to complain about.&quot;<br /> <br /> I already have trouble with direct statements of what material from the books says because I feel like I'm being condescending when I'm explaining things that I think are obvious. Attempting to guilt me for holding you accountable for reading the lore on the thing you're talking about is counterproductive.<br /> <br /> In addition: Internet, textual medium, tone, reading difficulty thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-21-2013, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:11:05-08:00","id":15189,"title":"","content":"I've thought about the possibility of a zombie lineage, although not in the voodoo sense, but in the modern movie disease kind.<br /> <br /> However, thematically, I would point out that in the lore you've based this one, zombies are slave labor, making them closer to an alternate tammuz than anything else. A slave that broke free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:30:08-08:00","id":15197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=15189#post15189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've thought about the possibility of a zombie lineage, although not in the voodoo sense, but in the modern movie disease kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a second I wondered how that would work but now I'm wondering if that might function like a weirdly fruitful Extempore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:46:18-08:00","id":15209,"title":"","content":"Oh sure, Satchel, that would be one way to do it. Do you have antagonists? It has the zombie rules, and not including all those supernaturals who can make zombies, it gives zombies three origins.<br /> <br /> Mystical, which could certainly end up as something like the samedi suggested here.<br /> <br /> Cursed places, which would result in extempores certainly.<br /> <br /> And disease, which could also create an extempore, or since the disease can be man made could be something like the disease equivalent of the nuclear promethean. Someone takes the zombie plague and tinkers and tinkers with it until their obsession turns it into a generative act for a promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T02:57:45-08:00","id":15275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Benjamin Beard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan?p=15155#post15155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually exactly what I dislike about the Ulgan. A huge part of their generative process includes this thing that is not Demiurge, Promethean, the Principle, or Divine Fire but spirits. Which spirits are these that know how to create Prometheans? What are they doing when they're not creating Prometheans? Why do they want to create Prometheans? And even if all those questions have reasonable answers, it seems to really dilute the theme of the game to have 4 Lineages that are mostly focused on mortals and their relationship to them and then this 5th one that is hooked into all kinds of supernatural shenanigans a la animist spirits. In my experience of running Promethean the game is a love letter to the human condition and Ulgans make no interesting comment in that respect (in my opinion).</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits explicitly <i>don't </i>create Prometheans. That's the whole point! The Ulgan are unwelcome not just in the Flesh, but also in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> It more and more seems to me as if your understanding of what the Ulgan are isn't in line with the presentation of the lineage as per the books - this might be the reason as for why you don't feel they fit into the game.<br /> <br /> My problem with the Samedi is that they're not as broad, thematically, as the Ulgan - as an Ulgan, you get to play both the Necromancer and the Shaman, not just one of them. The Ulgan aren't just Orpheus and Samedi and Erlik and Inanna, they're broad enough to encompass the Silent Hill aesthetic of the Shadow in addition to the themes of death and victory over death already covered by the Nepri.<br /> <br /> But hey, it's your game.<br /> <br /> On the topic of what the Ulgan add to the game - they provide a perspective of what humanity means just as the other lineages do, only in the context of the Other, the things that are far outside of the human perspective - including death, but not limited to death. If the Golems are people we cannot help but see as slaves, and the Galatea are people we objectify sexually, the Ulgan are the weird scary homeless guys who talk to ghosts and things that aren't there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T09:26:26-08:00","id":15432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Satchel:</b> For a second I wondered how that would work but now I'm wondering if that might function like a weirdly fruitful Extempore. </div> </div> </div>I had the notion once of a &quot;drowner&quot; lineage whose progenitor was formed in a disastrous flood, and whose creation process involves bludgeoning (to simulate being tossed about by currents) and drowning the body's &quot;donor&quot; (so unlike most Prometheans, they have to kill said donor themselves for it to work). If you wanted to add a zombie vibe, it could have originated in Katrina.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Christian A:</b> On the topic of what the Ulgan add to the game - they provide a perspective of what humanity means just as the other lineages do, only in the context of the Other, the things that are far outside of the human perspective ... the Ulgan are the weird scary homeless guys who talk to ghosts and things that aren't there. </div> </div> </div>I like this. Their manner of creation also partakes of shamic initiations, and the mystical perspective of initiation as making you into a new being, turned literal in their case.<br /> <br /> Anyway, regarding this lineage, both the Tammuz and Osirians deal with death, but their genesis was in the attempt to resurrect a specific individual, and they don't deal with ghosts so much as remains. So, adding together what I said in response to Christian A, I think this lineage should be rooted in communication with ancestors and the dead in general, and becoming a medium capable of doing so - retain the initiation element, and give them a bestowment allowing controlled possession by a ghost - ie, the Promethean lets the ghost in, and the possession ends when she decides it does, not the ghost.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T22:25:43-08:00","id":22126,"title":"","content":"Having recently re-read the Promethean Core and now starting to re-read through the remainder of the line, I better understand the sentiment some posters have been giving me regarding the thematic overlap between the Samedi and the Osirians. I now feel more inclined to make Osirians the ectoplasm Lineage and creating an entirely new phlegmatic Lineage. I think some concepts of the Samedi are still worth playing with but the Lineage would be quite different. I like the idea of a series of dual-humoured Lineages, the Samedi being melancholic and ectoplasmic.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Or perhaps ectoplasm, like radiation, involves tainted humours rather than being a humour of its own. Osirians could be the ectoplasmic phlegmatic Lineage...I don't know yet though. Regardless I feel like Ulgans are beside the point of the whole game line and will continue to try to write them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":806,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","user":"Benjamin Beard","date":". 12-03-2013, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:16:26-08:00","id":26914,"title":"","content":"Why not just drop the Ulgans outright? Does there need to be an Ectoplasmic Humour, or five core Lineages? Just keep the Osirans as Phlegmatic and don\u2019t worry about Ectoplasmic. <br /> <br /> What you\u2019d be losing would be the Ulgan Bestowment, namely the ability to physically interact with ephemeral beings. That\u2019s easy enough to convert into a Spiritus Transmutation, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:16:06-08:00","id":28028,"title":"","content":"I'd actually be ok with dropping Ulgans outright (see we don't disagree on <i>everything</i>) though I'd prefer to drop them to a minor lineage (that is, a low population) because why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> Benjamin, maybe it's just that I haven't read the core for a bit but I feel that Osirens are are more about Osiris' aspect as a ruler than his aspect as lord of the dead. Anyway, I like the Samadi and even if only as a minor lineage there's room for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}